 },
 "note": "Every widget of the cluster-overview grid as a record (UI redesign M5). draw.body = \"record\": the element draws the record and the page's markup is retired under it (VeraDash.drawTile); draw.body = \"page\": the page draws the body by hand and its own updaters address it by id — the record owns the frame, and a note says why. A record tile reads its source through the element: read.map names the envelope's fields (the shape's container ← a path, a dict of things ← rows named by key, every other key ← a field of each row); a composite reads its subject once and its children take $subject.<path> slices of it, or read on their own. A tile the page has no markup for (events, health) is drawn from this file alone. Generated from the markup by the M5 slice; edit by hand from here.",
